insert into challenge (source, slug, title, source_url) values ('coding_challenges', 'challenge-bitcask', 'Build your own Bitcask', 'https://codingchallenges.fyi/challenges/challenge-bitcask') on conflict (source, slug) do nothing;
insert into milestone (challenge_id, position, title, summary) values ((select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask'), 1, 'From a flat file to an append-only log', 'Build the command-line tool on a flat file, then replace it with checksummed records appended to rotating log files.');
insert into milestone_concept (milestone_id, concept_id) select (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1), id from concept where slug in ('key-value-store', 'append-only-log', 'checksums', 'byte-order');
insert into step (milestone_id, position, title, est_minutes) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1), 1, 'A flat file first', 10);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt, snippet, answer_key, rubric) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 1), 'think', 'predict', 'Use the first version from the primer, which rewrites the whole table to cask.0 after every change, one key and value per line. You run set a 1, then set b 2, then set a 3. How many lines does cask.0 hold afterwards? Answer with one number.', null, '{"match":"number_exact","expected":2,"derivation":"The table in memory holds one value per key, so after the three sets it holds a with 3 and b with 2. The file is overwritten with the whole table each time, so it ends with one line per key: 2 lines. Proof script output: 2."}'::jsonb, null);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 1), 'build', 'build', 'Build a command-line tool, ccbitcask, that takes a database directory with -db and keeps its data in a file named cask.0 inside it, one Key:Value pair per line. After every set, write the whole table to the file, replacing what was there, and read the file on startup to fill the table. Setting Key to Value and then getting Key should print Value.');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 1), 'hint', '', 'The table keeps one value per key, and the file is a copy of the table.', 'generated');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 1), 'example', '', 'A whiteboard list of who has which room is wiped and rewritten whenever someone changes room, so it always shows one line per person.', 'generated');
insert into step (milestone_id, position, title, est_minutes) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1), 2, 'Records in bytes', 15);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt, snippet, answer_key, rubric) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 2), 'think', 'predict', 'In your record layout every size is written as a 4-byte little-endian number. A key is 258 bytes long. What is the first of the four bytes written for its key size? Answer with one number, in decimal.', null, '{"match":"number_exact","expected":2,"derivation":"258 is 1 times 256 plus 2, so its bytes are 2 and 1 followed by two zeros, from least to most significant. Little-endian writes the least significant byte first, so the first byte is 2. Big-endian would start with 0. Proof script output: 2."}'::jsonb, null);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 2), 'build', 'build', 'Replace the flat file with an append-only log. Each set adds one record to the end of the active file: a CRC-32 of the record''s other fields, written first, followed by those fields packed into bytes, such as the timestamp, the key size, the value size, the key and the value. Use little-endian numbers, which is what the challenge''s author believes Bitcask uses, and look at the file with xxd to check the bytes.');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 2), 'hint', '', 'Split 258 into how many whole 256s it holds and what is left over, then ask which part little-endian writes first.', 'generated');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 2), 'example', '', 'Writing a date as day, month, year puts the smallest part first, while year, month, day puts the largest part first. Both hold the same date.', 'generated');
insert into step (milestone_id, position, title, est_minutes) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1), 3, 'Rotate the active file', 15);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt, snippet, answer_key, rubric) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 3), 'think', 'trace', 'In this test every record is exactly 30 bytes and the size limit is 100 bytes. Before each append, if the record would take the active file past 100 bytes, the writer closes it and starts a new file. Starting from an empty database, you run 7 sets of different keys. How many data files exist afterwards? Answer with one number.', null, '{"match":"number_exact","expected":3,"derivation":"Three records make 90 bytes. A fourth would make 120, past the limit, so the writer closes the first file and starts the second. The same happens after the sixth record, so the seventh starts a third file. The files hold 3, 3 and 1 records. Proof script output: 3."}'::jsonb, null);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 3), 'build', 'build', 'Make the size limit configurable, and when a write would take the active file past it, close that file and open the next one, numbered after it. Use a limit of a few hundred bytes in tests, where Riak''s default is 2 GB. Closed files are never written again.');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 3), 'hint', '', 'Fill one file record by record and stop at the first record that would not fit.', 'generated');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 3), 'example', '', 'Lining up 40 cm boxes on shelves 100 cm long fits two to a shelf, because a third would make 120 cm, so the third box starts a new shelf.', 'generated');
insert into step (milestone_id, position, title, est_minutes) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1), 4, 'What the checksum covers', 15);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt, snippet, answer_key, rubric) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 4), 'think', 'spot_bug', 'This set writes a record with a checksum, but some damaged records still pass the check when they are read back, and a write can be lost after the user was told it succeeded. Find the problems and the fixes.', 'on set key, value:
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 4), 'build', 'build', 'Compute the CRC over every byte after it, and decide when a set counts as done, for example after flushing and syncing the file. Write a test that changes one byte of the key size in a record and checks that reading it fails the CRC.');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 4), 'hint', '', 'Change one byte of the key size by hand. Which of the stored numbers would notice?', 'generated');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1) and s.position = 4), 'example', '', 'A seal over only the contents of a parcel does not show that someone changed the address label.', 'generated');
insert into question (milestone_id, concept_id, position, prompt, rubric) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 1), null, 1, 'Explain why your store appends records instead of rewriting a file, what each record holds and in what order its bytes go, and how you would know a record was damaged.', '[{"id":"t1","concept":"key-value-store","point":"Rewriting the whole table after every change costs more as the data grows, while appending writes only the new record"},{"id":"t2","concept":"append-only-log","point":"Every set adds a record to the end of the active file, nothing written is changed, and a full file is closed and a new one started"},{"id":"t3","concept":"byte-order","point":"The sizes and timestamp are fixed-width numbers in an agreed byte order, little-endian, so any reader decodes them the same way"},{"id":"t4","concept":"checksums","point":"Each record starts with a CRC-32 over the rest of its bytes, which is computed again on reading, and a mismatch means the record is damaged"}]'::jsonb);
insert into milestone (challenge_id, position, title, summary) values ((select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask'), 2, 'The keydir, reads and deletes', 'Keep only metadata in memory, read values with one seek, and delete keys with tombstones.');
insert into milestone_concept (milestone_id, concept_id) select (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2), id from concept where slug in ('hash-index', 'append-only-log', 'tombstones');
insert into step (milestone_id, position, title, est_minutes) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2), 1, 'Metadata, not values', 15);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt, snippet, answer_key, rubric) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 1), 'think', 'predict', 'Use this layout: a 16-byte header holding the CRC, the timestamp, the key size and the value size, 4 bytes each, then the key, then the value. Starting with an empty cask.0, you run set a one, set b two, set a six. Counting from 0 at the start of the file, what value position does the keydir hold for a? Answer with one number.', null, '{"match":"number_exact","expected":57,"derivation":"Each record is 16 + 1 + 3 = 20 bytes, so the three records start at 0, 20 and 40. The keydir points at the latest record for a, the third. Its value starts after the 16-byte header and the 1-byte key: 40 + 16 + 1 = 57. Proof script output: 57."}'::jsonb, null);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 1), 'build', 'build', 'Change the hash table to hold metadata instead of the value: the file id, the value position, the value size and the timestamp. Every set appends a record and points the key''s entry at the new one.');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 1), 'hint', '', 'Find where the latest record for a starts, then step over everything that comes before its value.', 'generated');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 1), 'example', '', 'A library catalogue card holds the shelf and position of a book, not the book. When a new edition arrives, the card is changed to point at the new copy.', 'generated');
insert into step (milestone_id, position, title, est_minutes) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2), 2, 'Read with one seek', 15);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt, snippet, answer_key, rubric) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 2), 'think', 'spot_bug', 'This get works in a fresh database but returns wrong values or crashes once there are several files. Find the two problems.', 'on get key:
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 2), 'build', 'build', 'Make get look up the key''s entry, open the file it names, seek to the value position and read value size bytes. Test with enough keys to spread over several files, and check that updating a key appends a new record and that get then returns the new value.');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 2), 'hint', '', 'Set a key, write enough other keys to fill a file, then get the first key. Which file holds it?', 'generated');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 2), 'example', '', 'A filing cabinet with several drawers needs both the drawer and the folder number. The folder number alone sends you to the wrong drawer.', 'generated');
insert into step (milestone_id, position, title, est_minutes) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2), 3, 'Delete with tombstones', 15);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt, snippet, answer_key, rubric) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 3), 'think', 'predict', 'Starting with an empty database, you run set a 1, set b 2, del a, set c 3, del b. No merge has run. How many records are in the log? Answer with one number.', null, '{"match":"number_exact","expected":5,"derivation":"The log is append-only, so a delete cannot remove anything. Each del appends a tombstone record instead. Three sets and two deletes make 5 records, although only c still has a value. Proof script output: 5."}'::jsonb, null);
insert into task (step_id, role, kind, prompt) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 3), 'build', 'build', 'Add a del command that appends a tombstone record and marks the key as deleted in the keydir, or removes its entry. Make get never return a deleted key: after set Key Value, get prints Value, and after del Key, get prints nil.');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 3), 'hint', '', 'Can an append-only file make an old record go away? What does it write instead?', 'generated');
insert into hint (step_id, level, language, body, content_status) values ((select s.id from step s where s.milestone_id = (select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2) and s.position = 3), 'example', '', 'In a paper ledger you never rub out an entry. To cancel a payment you add a new line saying it was cancelled.', 'generated');
insert into question (milestone_id, concept_id, position, prompt, rubric) values ((select m.id from milestone m where m.challenge_id = (select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask') and m.position = 2), null, 1, 'Walk through what happens on disk and in memory when you set a key, update it, read it and then delete it.', '[{"id":"t1","concept":"append-only-log","point":"The set and the update each append a record, and the old record stays in the file"},{"id":"t2","concept":"hash-index","point":"The keydir holds the file id, value position, value size and timestamp of the latest record, so get is one lookup, one seek and one read"},{"id":"t3","concept":"tombstones","point":"Delete appends a tombstone and marks or removes the keydir entry, so get returns nil, and replaying the log later still sees the key as deleted"}]'::jsonb);
insert into milestone (challenge_id, position, title, summary) values ((select id from challenge where source = 'coding_challenges' and slug = 'challenge-bitcask'), 3, 'Merge, hint files and recovery', 'Compact closed files into live data only, write hint files for fast startup, and recover from a crash mid-write.');
