        pc = position of the previous "[" before pc
    pc = pc + 1', null, '[{"id":"p1","point":"Jumping to the next or previous bracket ignores nesting, so with a loop inside a loop the jump lands on the inner loop''s bracket"},{"id":"p2","point":"Pairing the brackets with a stack, or counting how deep it is while scanning, finds the matching bracket instead"},{"id":"p3","point":"An unbalanced program, such as a closing bracket with no opening one, is never detected, so the search finds nothing and the interpreter misbehaves; it should check the pairs before running and report an error"}]'::jsonb);
