print_all(sort(lines, random_compare))', null, '[{"id":"p1","point":"The answers are not consistent, the same pair can be compared twice and get opposite answers, so the sort may misbehave and some orders come out far more often than others"},{"id":"p2","point":"Two equal lines are not treated as equal, so they can end up far apart, which breaks the rule that equal lines stay together"},{"id":"p3","point":"The fix is to give each line one random key, such as a hash with a seed chosen for the run, and sort by that key"}]'::jsonb);

